Cyclo for Ubuntu and Debian
---------------------------

Cyclo is a per-user host CLI. Installing this package does not start a daemon,
create a service account, add users to the docker group, or create Docker
containers, networks, or volumes.

Runtime prerequisites
---------------------

The package depends on Git, Docker Engine, and the separately packaged DComp
command. The invoking user must be able to access Docker and must not run Cyclo
as root. Confirm that DComp exposes machine API 1 before the first stateful
Cyclo command:

    dcomp version --json
    cyclo doctor

Configuration and credentials
-----------------------------

With the default state root, Cyclo reads /etc/cyclo/host.conf. The packaged file
is a conffile and is intentionally comment-only; leaving it empty routes teams
directly to Cyclo's credential gateway. Put only provider-component declarations
there. Do not put API keys or OAuth tokens in that file.

Cyclo keeps state below ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/cyclo. It stores
provider credentials in a private Docker volume, never in /etc or /var/lib.
Use --state-root (or CYCLO_STATE_ROOT) when an installation needs independent
state and a local host.conf.
